> User eeisner (281731)
Request Time: 1 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":{"State":"open","OpenTime":0,"CloseTime":0,"IsApproved":true,"IsPinned":false,"IsDeleted":false,"IsHidden":false,"IsArchived":false,"IsFollowing":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanReply":true,"CanFollow":true,"TotalPosts":33,"QueuedPosts":0,"DeletedPosts":0,"HasUnreadPosts":true,"HasAttachments":false,"Views":1403,"MovedTo":null,"MovedOn":0,"FirstPostId":1885327,"Rating":0,"RatingHits":0,"Starter":{"Id":281922,"Name":"AliciaW","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281922.jpg?_r=1424557167","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"IsOnline":false},"StartDate":1423141105,"LastPoster":{"Id":282367,"Name":"MNsunseeker","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"PollState":"0","LastVote":0,"ForumId":14,"Preview":{"Id":1885327,"PostDate":1423141105,"PostContent":"We just got engaged last week and have already decided we want to do a destination wedding! We're...","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"xoliciaxo@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"108.180.31.5","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1422468085,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281922.jpg?_r=1424557167","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"FormattedName":"AliciaW","Id":281922,"Name":"AliciaW","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"108.180.31.5","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"2d5b99e880031bf745997280d1b07aa6","RawContent":"We just got engaged last week and have already decided we want to do a destination wedding! We&#039;re thinking Mexico because it&#039;s probably the most affordable for everyone coming. I&#039;m just wondering what the average price is for a wedding in Mexico. And does anyone have any suggestions for great resorts with more affordable wedding packages? Any advice helps here as we&#039;re just starting to look. Thanks!","Attachments":[],"Id":1885327,"PostDate":1423141105,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                We just got engaged last week and have already decided we want to do a destination wedding! We're thinking Mexico because it's probably the most affordable for everyone coming. I'm just wondering what the average price is for a wedding in Mexico. And does anyone have any suggestions for great resorts with more affordable wedding packages? Any advice helps here as we're just starting to look. Thanks!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"xoliciaxo@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"108.180.31.5","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1422468085,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281922.jpg?_r=1424557167","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"FormattedName":"AliciaW","Id":281922,"Name":"AliciaW","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"107.77.87.34","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7e65bf3992d23e30fd4a20575bdfbd97","RawContent":"@[member=\"AliciaW\"] Congratulations! A wedding can be expensive or affordable anywhere you decide to get married. A misconception that I&#039;ve come to realize that having a wedding in Mexico is going to be cheaper. Definitely not true. Especially when you start to add up extras and if you have more than 15 or 20 guests (the average covered in a wedding package), the price adds up very quickly. \n\n\nAlso depending on when you want your wedding \u2013 if you decide to come during the high season you should expect to pay more but have a really good chance at good weather. Versus the low season, the fall, prices will be cheaper but there&#039;s a higher chance that you&#039;ll have rain on your wedding day. \n\n\nI would definitely get a travel agent to start. They can give you some great recommendations on hotels. Also start thinking about the kind of hotel you want and the size of your wedding. All-inclusive like dreams, palace, Iberostars, Barcelo vs non AI like Rosewood\/Banyan tree mayakoba. Adults only or family friendly? Church ceremony or beach? What is important to you \u2013 a good night life such as in downtown Cancun or Playa del Carmen, more rustic Mexico like Tulum, a good beach? Also think about distance from the airport. A hotel in Cancun is a 10 minute drive, versus the Barcelo complex is an hour and a half south and Tulum even farther.\n\n\nIn my opinion, choosing the resort is the most stressful part. After that, it&#039;s all fun :-) good luck and don&#039;t hesitate with any questions!","Attachments":[],"Id":1885339,"PostDate":1423146225,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281922\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281922-aliciaw\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">AliciaW<\/span><\/a> Congratulations! A wedding can be expensive or affordable anywhere you decide to get married. A misconception that I've come to realize that having a wedding in Mexico is going to be cheaper. Definitely not true. Especially when you start to add up extras and if you have more than 15 or 20 guests (the average covered in a wedding package), the price adds up very quickly. <br><br>\nAlso depending on when you want your wedding \u2013 if you decide to come during the high season you should expect to pay more but have a really good chance at good weather. Versus the low season, the fall, prices will be cheaper but there's a higher chance that you'll have rain on your wedding day. <br><br>\nI would definitely get a travel agent to start. They can give you some great recommendations on hotels. Also start thinking about the kind of hotel you want and the size of your wedding. All-inclusive like dreams, palace, Iberostars, Barcelo vs non AI like Rosewood\/Banyan tree mayakoba. Adults only or family friendly? Church ceremony or beach? What is important to you \u2013 a good night life such as in downtown Cancun or Playa del Carmen, more rustic Mexico like Tulum, a good beach? Also think about distance from the airport. A hotel in Cancun is a 10 minute drive, versus the Barcelo complex is an hour and a half south and Tulum even farther.<br><br>\nIn my opinion, choosing the resort is the most stressful part. After that, it's all fun :-) good luck and don't hesitate with any questions!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"natalie.zaval@gmail.com","IpAddress":"67.184.87.109","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1389113752,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275926.jpg?_r=1418313578","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"nattiegams325","Id":275926,"Name":"nattiegams325","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"24.89.236.44","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f2de9c8cf7f884fce944f310a89ce5ec","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congratulations and welcome.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1885367,"PostDate":1423155528,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congratulations and welcome.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"njwood000@gmail.com","IpAddress":"71.7.173.185","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1405806791,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"Msmimi","Id":279087,"Name":"Msmimi","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"69.47.187.120","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"245cf6b6f6a96743e63715de9824cce0","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"AliciaW\"] - I completely agree with @[member=\"nattiegams325\"]. Also be sure to gather as much information as you can about the types of wedding packages offered and that includes what kinds of things cost extra. While you should always be prepared for a few unexpected expenses, I have read on here that some resorts have charged extra for things like chairs for the ceremony and then charged another fee for moving those same chairs to the reception location! (That seems absurd to me, by the way.) Everyone has a different budget and expectations, so knowing more of this info in advance will help planning go more smoothly. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1885397,"PostDate":1423169136,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281922\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281922-aliciaw\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">AliciaW<\/span><\/a> - I completely agree with @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"275926\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/275926-nattiegams325\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">nattiegams325<\/span><\/a>. Also be sure to gather as much information as you can about the types of wedding packages offered and that includes what kinds of things cost extra. While you should always be prepared for a few unexpected expenses, I have read on here that some resorts have charged extra for things like chairs for the ceremony and then charged another fee for moving those same chairs to the reception location! (That seems absurd to me, by the way.) Everyone has a different budget and expectations, so knowing more of this info in advance will help planning go more smoothly. \u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jhowe114@gmail.com","IpAddress":"38.98.131.98","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1402408389,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278395.jpg?_r=1421871115","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":285,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"JenniferH114","Id":278395,"Name":"JenniferH114","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.72.4.186","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"bff15db0fb4b880ff38985d6098c76c3","RawContent":"Our wedding package for 40 people will cost us about $6500 US. Riviera Maya in mid-April. Plus everything else (wardrobe, photography, stationary, gifts, and other misc costs) we&#039;re budgeting total cost to be around $15000. I over-budgeted for a lot of things so our cost will probably be closer to $13000 all-in.","Attachments":[],"Id":1885398,"PostDate":1423169628,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Our wedding package for 40 people will cost us about $6500 US. Riviera Maya in mid-April. Plus everything else (wardrobe, photography, stationary, gifts, and other misc costs) we're budgeting total cost to be around $15000. I over-budgeted for a lot of things so our cost will probably be closer to $13000 all-in. \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"tinsisienmay@gmail.com","IpAddress":"184.71.74.195","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1413538355,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"starbx123","Id":280691,"Name":"starbx123","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"96.48.159.21","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8eca1214a849c8b2d25c0b0381ae8bb2","RawContent":"@[member=\"AliciaW\"] I agreements what everyone has said so far and they&#039;ve covered a lot of very important points. I don&#039;t know if you&#039;re from Canada but if you are, you&#039;ll also have to factor in the exchange rates. Especially since the Canadian dollar is quite low right now.","Attachments":[],"Id":1885399,"PostDate":1423171128,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281922\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281922-aliciaw\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">AliciaW<\/span><\/a> I agreements what everyone has said so far and they've covered a lot of very important points. I don't know if you're from Canada but if you are, you'll also have to factor in the exchange rates. Especially since the Canadian dollar is quite low right now.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jerilee.valenzuela@shaw.ca","IpAddress":"24.114.26.77","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1410080585,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279721.jpg?_r=1420071985","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Wafflesmom","Id":279721,"Name":"Wafflesmom","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"<strong>Edited by calgarybride2015, 05 February 2015 - 09:54 PM.<\/strong>","EditDate":1423173256,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"05b6a5ddd6e614bb9e9aab1c9ef22d9a","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;The resort I got married at has very reasonable wedding packages. &amp;nbsp;Their extras are very affordable and they don&#039;t nickle and dime you for setting things up and the like.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We had a wedding of 45 people. We took the free package and did all the upgrades we wanted. We went with the private beach and palapa for the reception. We had a lot of extra flowers (upgraded bouquets, bridesmaids bouquets, bouts for men, petals to sprinkle), mariachi band, had an extra 4 hours for our reception\/open bar, cocktail hour, chair ribbons, mariachi, DJ for 6 hours, and with my hair trail, and wedding day hair\/makeup I only paid $5000 after deposit. This also included some nice honeymoon items. &amp;nbsp; What was nice also is that our resort charged in pesos (helps with the horrible Canadian dollar) and tax was included - some brides get an extra 16% tacked on. &amp;nbsp;All my decor was put out for free and they didn&#039;t charge us to move chairs, etc. around&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;She also threw in somethings for free!! &amp;nbsp;Isle runner, Chinese lighted lanterns, etc.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The free wedding package was in an A&#039;la Carte which I hadn&#039;t envisioned for my wedding, but some people do. &amp;nbsp;They have about 5 wedding packages you can choose from ranging from like $1800 (if you don&#039;t get it for free) to around $5000. &amp;nbsp;Lots of the larger packages had fluff we didn&#039;t need so we found it easier to go basic and just upgrade what we wanted.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;There are definitely great resorts out there with affordable wedding packages, you just have to look for them!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1885401,"PostDate":1423172522,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>The resort I got married at has very reasonable wedding packages. \u00a0Their extras are very affordable and they don't nickle and dime you for setting things up and the like.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We had a wedding of 45 people. We took the free package and did all the upgrades we wanted. We went with the private beach and palapa for the reception. We had a lot of extra flowers (upgraded bouquets, bridesmaids bouquets, bouts for men, petals to sprinkle), mariachi band, had an extra 4 hours for our reception\/open bar, cocktail hour, chair ribbons, mariachi, DJ for 6 hours, and with my hair trail, and wedding day hair\/makeup I only paid $5000 after deposit. This also included some nice honeymoon items. \u00a0 What was nice also is that our resort charged in pesos (helps with the horrible Canadian dollar) and tax was included - some brides get an extra 16% tacked on. \u00a0All my decor was put out for free and they didn't charge us to move chairs, etc. around<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>She also threw in somethings for free!! \u00a0Isle runner, Chinese lighted lanterns, etc.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The free wedding package was in an A'la Carte which I hadn't envisioned for my wedding, but some people do. \u00a0They have about 5 wedding packages you can choose from ranging from like $1800 (if you don't get it for free) to around $5000. \u00a0Lots of the larger packages had fluff we didn't need so we found it easier to go basic and just upgrade what we wanted.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>There are definitely great resorts out there with affordable wedding packages, you just have to look for them!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399410602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"190.167.10.35","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c7ef35dea50150977cbf3939d90b31fa","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congrats on your engagement, AliciaW and plans for a destination wedding!!!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Our incomparable Mayan Riviera is a very popular choice for numerous wedding couples, for many reasons. Here are a few visual ones.....with more at this link: &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10150695320839487.414941.18683524486&amp;amp;type=3&#039;&gt;Cover Photos&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-a-iad.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfa1\/v\/t1.0-9\/p417x417\/10354809_10152664882419487_1728880669268284102_n.jpg?oh=55fb5560d2e78b652f86d2620fa939aa&amp;amp;oe=556B0E32\" alt=\"10354809_10152664882419487_1728880669268\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/fbcdn-sphotos-h-a.akamaihd.net\/hphotos-ak-xpf1\/t31.0-8\/10514196_10152534166149487_1439571747332471489_o.jpg\" alt=\"10514196_10152534166149487_1439571747332\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=\"https:\/\/scontent-b-iad.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xpf1\/t31.0-8\/10264266_10152377393459487_387743739374526349_o.jpg\" alt=\"10264266_10152377393459487_3877437393745\"&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Wishing you happy research, and all the best with your journey - Enjoy, cheers!!! team MTM :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1885477,"PostDate":1423236220,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congrats on your engagement, AliciaW and plans for a destination wedding!!!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Our incomparable Mayan Riviera is a very popular choice for numerous wedding couples, for many reasons. Here are a few visual ones.....with more at this link: <a href='https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/media\/set\/?set=a.10150695320839487.414941.18683524486&type=3' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Cover Photos<\/a><\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-a-iad.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xfa1\/v\/t1.0-9\/p417x417\/10354809_10152664882419487_1728880669268284102_n.jpg?oh=55fb5560d2e78b652f86d2620fa939aa&oe=556B0E32\" alt=\"10354809_10152664882419487_1728880669268\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/fbcdn-sphotos-h-a.akamaihd.net\/hphotos-ak-xpf1\/t31.0-8\/10514196_10152534166149487_1439571747332471489_o.jpg\" alt=\"10514196_10152534166149487_1439571747332\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"https:\/\/scontent-b-iad.xx.fbcdn.net\/hphotos-xpf1\/t31.0-8\/10264266_10152377393459487_387743739374526349_o.jpg\" alt=\"10264266_10152377393459487_3877437393745\"><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wishing you happy research, and all the best with your journey - Enjoy, cheers!!! team MTM <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><img src=\"http:\/\/i711.photobucket.com\/albums\/ww116\/momentsthatmatter\/MTMLogo08-1.png\" alt=\"MTMLogo08-1.png\"><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.momentsthatmatterphotography.com'><strong><span style=\"font-size:18px;\">Moments That Matter Photography Studios, Playa del Carmen, Mexico<\/span><\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Canadian Award Winning Photojournalist serving Mayan Riviera<br>\nEmail: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='mailto:contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com'>contact@momentsthatmatterphotography.com<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Scoop on what we do:\u00a0 <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/reviews\/r\/4212-beautiful-november-wedding\/#review'>MTM Reviews<\/a><\/p>\n<p>Meet Lincoln & Team MTM: <a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/vimeo.com\/51032621'>\"Meet Lincoln\" Video + see his Passion!!!<\/a>","Email":"momentsthatmatterphotography@gmail.com","IpAddress":"189.221.252.187","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1280192660,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230711.png?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Moments That Matter","Id":230711,"Name":"Moments That Matter","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"308f8e5e8b567cace9c38d28f194d821","RawContent":"[quote name=\"AliciaW\" post=\"1885327\" timestamp=\"1423159105\"]\nWe just got engaged last week and have already decided we want to do a destination wedding! We&#039;re thinking Mexico because it&#039;s probably the most affordable for everyone coming. I&#039;m just wondering what the average price is for a wedding in Mexico. And does anyone have any suggestions for great resorts with more affordable wedding packages? Any advice helps here as we&#039;re just starting to look. Thanks![\/quote]Congrats!\nMy Fiance and I got engaged in Mexico back in October and we&#039;ve always known we would have a destination wedding.\nWe are having ours at Beach Palace, Cancun.\nIt also depends on the time of year that you choose because the Caribbean has shoulder seasons which are lower in price and high seasons.\n\nWe chose December 10-17 and our price is currently $1663 per person, but with a one time price drop guarantee.\nThe reason we chose Palace is because we have been there and they are outstanding quality resorts. Also, if you book so many rooms you get unlimited private events while you&#039;re there :)\n[quote name=\"calgarybride2015\" post=\"1885401\" timestamp=\"1423190522\"]\nThe resort I got married at has very reasonable wedding packages.  Their extras are very affordable and they don&#039;t nickle and dime you for setting things up and the like.\n\nWe had a wedding of 45 people. We took the free package and did all the upgrades we wanted. We went with the private beach and palapa for the reception. We had a lot of extra flowers (upgraded bouquets, bridesmaids bouquets, bouts for men, petals to sprinkle), mariachi band, had an extra 4 hours for our reception\/open bar, cocktail hour, chair ribbons, mariachi, DJ for 6 hours, and with my hair trail, and wedding day hair\/makeup I only paid $5000 after deposit. This also included some nice honeymoon items.   What was nice also is that our resort charged in pesos (helps with the horrible Canadian dollar) and tax was included - some brides get an extra 16% tacked on.  All my decor was put out for free and they didn&#039;t charge us to move chairs, etc. around\n\nShe also threw in somethings for free!!  Isle runner, Chinese lighted lanterns, etc.\n\nThe free wedding package was in an A&#039;la Carte which I hadn&#039;t envisioned for my wedding, but some people do.  They have about 5 wedding packages you can choose from ranging from like $1800 (if you don&#039;t get it for free) to around $5000.  Lots of the larger packages had fluff we didn&#039;t need so we found it easier to go basic and just upgrade what we wanted. \n\nThere are definitely great resorts out there with affordable wedding packages, you just have to look for them![\/quote]Wow, that&#039;s awesome! I&#039;ve started running into more and more cost as I go along (like the chair movement fee) and it seems never ending. I love that you were able to pay in pesos.. My resorts is looking for USD payments. I am over budgeting because I have a strong feeling it&#039;s going to cost me more than I had originally planned for.","Attachments":[],"Id":1885481,"PostDate":1423236595,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>AliciaW, on 05 February 2015 - 12:58 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>We just got engaged last week and have already decided we want to do a destination wedding! We're thinking Mexico because it's probably the most affordable for everyone coming. I'm just wondering what the average price is for a wedding in Mexico. And does anyone have any suggestions for great resorts with more affordable wedding packages? Any advice helps here as we're just starting to look. Thanks!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Congrats!<br>\nMy Fiance and I got engaged in Mexico back in October and we've always known we would have a destination wedding.<\/p>\n<p>We are having ours at Beach Palace, Cancun.<\/p>\n<p>It also depends on the time of year that you choose because the Caribbean has shoulder seasons which are lower in price and high seasons.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We chose December 10-17 and our price is currently $1663 per person, but with a one time price drop guarantee.<\/p>\n<p>The reason we chose Palace is because we have been there and they are outstanding quality resorts. Also, if you book so many rooms you get unlimited private events while you're there <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p><br \/><p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>calgarybride2015, on 05 February 2015 - 09:42 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>The resort I got married at has very reasonable wedding packages. \u00a0Their extras are very affordable and they don't nickle and dime you for setting things up and the like.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We had a wedding of 45 people. We took the free package and did all the upgrades we wanted. We went with the private beach and palapa for the reception. We had a lot of extra flowers (upgraded bouquets, bridesmaids bouquets, bouts for men, petals to sprinkle), mariachi band, had an extra 4 hours for our reception\/open bar, cocktail hour, chair ribbons, mariachi, DJ for 6 hours, and with my hair trail, and wedding day hair\/makeup I only paid $5000 after deposit. This also included some nice honeymoon items. \u00a0 What was nice also is that our resort charged in pesos (helps with the horrible Canadian dollar) and tax was included - some brides get an extra 16% tacked on. \u00a0All my decor was put out for free and they didn't charge us to move chairs, etc. around<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>She also threw in somethings for free!! \u00a0Isle runner, Chinese lighted lanterns, etc.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The free wedding package was in an A'la Carte which I hadn't envisioned for my wedding, but some people do. \u00a0They have about 5 wedding packages you can choose from ranging from like $1800 (if you don't get it for free) to around $5000. \u00a0Lots of the larger packages had fluff we didn't need so we found it easier to go basic and just upgrade what we wanted.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>There are definitely great resorts out there with affordable wedding packages, you just have to look for them!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Wow, that's awesome! I've started running into more and more cost as I go along (like the chair movement fee) and it seems never ending. I love that you were able to pay in pesos.. My resorts is looking for USD payments. I am over budgeting because I have a strong feeling it's going to cost me more than I had originally planned for.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a>","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1419419814,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1425000950","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"166.137.12.126","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78741,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"200a8dc0c43f5675332216860c33c8ea","RawContent":"Congrats! Something to consider is NOT choosing a resort. We decided to just let everyone choose where they wanted\/could stay and then we chose to have our wedding at a beach club. Don&#039;t let beach club scare you. The beautiful beach club we chose did not have a rental fee, and you could get prices for about 40-50 bucks per person. Obviously you can customize it and the price would vary. We wanted to customize it so we are able to have whatever food we want, whatever dj, florist, baker, photographer we want, officiant etc and have to pay ZERO extra vendor fees!\n\n\nAdditionally we don&#039;t have to run around crazy worrying about people booking rooms, which seems to be a common stressor I see on here. \n\n\nAnd we don&#039;t have to have our guests pay an exorbitant amount of money for a room while providing the option for those who do.\n\n\nJust a thought.\n\n\nHave fun!!","Attachments":[],"Id":1885500,"PostDate":1423242972,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Congrats! Something to consider is NOT choosing a resort. We decided to just let everyone choose where they wanted\/could stay and then we chose to have our wedding at a beach club. Don't let beach club scare you. The beautiful beach club we chose did not have a rental fee, and you could get prices for about 40-50 bucks per person. Obviously you can customize it and the price would vary. We wanted to customize it so we are able to have whatever food we want, whatever dj, florist, baker, photographer we want, officiant etc and have to pay ZERO extra vendor fees!<br><br>\nAdditionally we don't have to run around crazy worrying about people booking rooms, which seems to be a common stressor I see on here. <br><br>\nAnd we don't have to have our guests pay an exorbitant amount of money for a room while providing the option for those who do.<br><br>\nJust a thought.<br><br>\nHave fun!! \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"lisananth@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"166.137.101.169","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1401118433,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-278120.jpg?_r=1421810202","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","Id":278120,"Name":"LisaAnthonyPoppy","IsOnline":false}}],"Id":"78741","Title":"Newbie Here! Average Mexico Wedding Costs?","LastPostDate":1426198150},"Pages":{"TotalItems":33,"TotalPages":4,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":10,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":30},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
